**`instance/doctor` — one positional, two meanings**

**Context.** `viva instance/doctor <one>` has to guess whether `<one>` is an instance or an env filter. It guesses "instance" only if the record resolves it. If not, the token quietly becomes a filter over whatever instance your session is on. After `instance/delete tapped`, the record no longer has `tapped`, so it becomes a filter on hello-world. You get hello-world's full report with the env rows narrowed to nothing, and no error.

