**Inspector.svelte**: the effect re-ran itself forever on mount. Now it reruns only when `row` changes.

Cause: `commons/instances/hello-world/app/Inspector.svelte:5`. The effect reads `held` (for `held?.seen`) and then writes `held`. Reading it makes `held` a dependency, so every write schedules another run. Svelte stops the loop and throws `effect_update_depth_exceeded`.

Fix: read the previous `seen` inside `untrack`, so `row` is the only thing the effect depends on.

```svelte
// commons/instances/hello-world/app/Inspector.svelte
 <script>
+  import { untrack } from "svelte";
   let { row } = $props();
   let held = $state(null);
   $effect(() => {
-    held = { ...row, seen: (held?.seen ?? 0) + 1 };
+    const snapshot = { ...row };
+    held = { ...snapshot, seen: untrack(() => held?.seen ?? 0) + 1 };
   });
 </script>
```

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- In Svelte 5, an `$effect` depends on every reactive value it reads while running. Reading and writing the same `$state` inside one effect always loops.
- `untrack(fn)` reads a value without subscribing to it. That fits here because `seen` is a history counter, not an input.
- Spreading `{ ...row }` reads every field of the `row` proxy. So the effect also reruns when a single field of `row` changes, not just when `row` is replaced.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

